# The first seconds of every emulator ES-DE launches on the Deck (M16 item 4), filmed by boot-capture.sh:
# SYSTEM EMULATOR CORE|- SECONDS -- ROM-GLOB. The owner saw GameCube games start at the right size, drop to a
# third of the screen in the top left, and come back; each standalone emulator and RetroArch is filmed once.
# The OSD round (2026-10-06): no emulator's own box, toast or banner over the composed picture either: not
# Flycast's Starting... box, Cemu's shader cache progress and counts (its boot image stays), PPSSPP's top-centre
# toast or RetroArch's load-content banner; the picture black until the game draws.
gc dolphin - 30 -- Legend of Zelda, The - The Wind Waker (USA).rvz
wii dolphin - 30 -- New Super Mario Bros. Wii*.wbfs
ps2 pcsx2 - 30 -- Def Jam - Fight for NY (USA).iso
dreamcast flycast - 25 -- Sonic Adventure (USA) (En,Ja,Fr,De,Es) (Rev A).chd
n3ds azahar - 30 -- Legend of Zelda, The - Ocarina of Time 3D*.3ds
wiiu cemu - 40 -- MARIO KART 8 (US).wua
# Ryujinx films 70 s: on 2026-10-06 the Deck took 10 s to load the game from the SD card and 10.5 s to recompile its
# PPTC cache, so the 40 s film ended on Ryujinx's loading view (PPTC 20987 of 22500) before the game's first frame,
# where the size is judged; the window tree showed the Vulkan child at 1278x706+0+35 in the 1280x800 window there.
# Filmed for 130 s on 2026-10-06 (M16's Deck probe): with the translation cache warm the game's first frame composed at
# 45.5 s, when Ryujinx made the swapchain it presents (1280x800) and the child grew to 1280x800+0+0; the 1278x706 child
# exists only behind Ryujinx's own loading view, and the picture is 1280x720 at 0,40. A cold cache (the first run after
# Ryujinx changes) reached the game at 113 s: film that one for 130 s.
switch ryujinx - 70 -- Animal Crossing New Horizons*.nsp
psp ppsspp - 20 -- Ape Escape - On the Loose (USA).iso
nds melonds - 20 -- Advance Wars - Dual Strike (USA, Australia).zip
# Beetle PSX reports its 256x240 placeholder, then 640x472, with a 478-line blip at the Sony logo (about 20 s): the TV
# holds still through all of them, sized for the PS1's 240 lines (RendererNominalFrame), the 472 lines in its 480-row
# frame with 4 black rows above and below (judge the bezel's corner in the shots before and after each change).
psx retroarch mednafen_psx 25 -- Crash Bandicoot (USA).m3u
